From 8e8927cef440156d7c8a0a358c8a8677a40cb41e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:25:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 151/206] analyze_snapshot: extract ARM64 immediate
 reconstruction into a testable header

F66 needs to reconstruct the immediates of the two dispatch-table call heads
that DecodeDispatchCall currently reports as kNoSelector. ARM64 immediate
decoding is easy to get subtly wrong in a way that still yields plausible
numbers, so the arithmetic moves somewhere a unit test can reach it.

The header is deliberately free of VM dependencies so that
spikes/shorebird_linkinfo_oracle/test_arm64_decode.cc can include THIS source
rather than a transcription of it. A test built on a re-typed copy passes while
the shipped binary is wrong.

DecodeImmLogical is dart::Instr::ImmLogical (constants_arm64.h:1618) unchanged;
it is only relocated here. New: ApplyMoveWide (movz/movn/movk), ApplyAddShift
and DecodeLogicalImmediateToReg, which is strict where the shape matcher is
loose -- it refuses and/eor/ands and any non-xzr Rn, because the value in the
register is then not a function of the words this scanner has seen.

No behaviour change yet: nothing includes this header.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/runtime/vm/analyze_snapshot_arm64_decode.h b/runtime/vm/analyze_snapshot_arm64_decode.h
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..a5d1558f376
--- /dev/null
+++ b/runtime/vm/analyze_snapshot_arm64_decode.h
@@ -0,0 +1,136 @@
